PREDECESSOR / SEAM NOTES (covenant #3, #7 — no skip-and-assume, no bypass)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* P1/S8 state-holders: only a representative `VehicleSettingsModel` ships today;
  there is no fleet-analytics/vehicle-list holder wired in `AppContainer`
  (bootstrap is documented "future"). The surface binds through a
  `FleetStatsDataSource` seam (same dependency-inversion `VehicleSettingsModel`
  uses) + a concrete `StateHolderFleetStatsDataSource` built on the existing
  `StateHolderModel` / `LoadableState` primitives. The host injects the holder
  models once they land — the view itself does NO HTTP.
* P1/S10 i18n: the native catalog (Localization/Localizable.xcstrings) does not
  yet contain the web `dashboard:fleet.*` keys (it is outside this surface's
  allowed file set). Strings use `LocalizedStringResource(key, defaultValue:)` /
  `String(localized:defaultValue:)` — the exact native analogue of the web
  `t(key, default)` pattern — so the key is the source of truth and the build's
  Swift string-extraction will populate the catalog. Keys are centralized in
  `FleetStatsStrings` for audit.
* P1/S11 diagnostics: no native diagnostics sink exists yet; the surface defines
  a minimal `FleetStatsDiagnostics` seam + privacy-aware `os.Logger` default and
  emits `view.opened` (slug "FleetStatsWidget") exactly once. Swap for the shared
  sink when it lands.

